# ---------------------------------------------------------------- environment
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.bak
*.bak-*
.superpowers/

# --------------------------------------------------- READING MATERIAL, PRIVATE
# Books, papers and MIDI libraries collected for reference: 112 000 files and
# 4.8 GB of third-party work. None of it is ours to redistribute, and walking
# it makes every git command crawl.
to-read/

# ------------------------------------------------------ THE CORPUS IS PRIVATE
#
# refs/ and corpus_versions/ hold songs and presets written by a real Deluge.
# They are NOT published, for two independent reasons:
#
#   1. they are somebody's music;
#   2. a Deluge song embeds the complete parameter set of every instrument it
#      uses, so a song made with a paid preset redistributes that preset.
#
# The rules below are deliberately deny-by-default: everything under refs/ is
# ignored, and only the single file that is firmware defaults is let back in.
# Populate these folders from your own SD card — see README, "Bring your own
# corpus". Nothing you drop there will be committed by accident.
refs/*
!refs/synths/
refs/synths/*
!refs/synths/TEMPL.XML

corpus_versions/

# Generated schema inventories. They are built FROM the corpus, and their
# "observed values" columns quote song names, preset names and sample paths
# taken straight out of it. Regenerate them against your own corpus with
# tools/extract_schema.py.
docs/SCHEMA_song_*.md
docs/SCHEMA_kit_*.md

# ------------------------------------------------------------ generated files
# Songs produced by the tools. They reproduce by running the tools again, and
# some of them are failed experiments kept only while they were useful.
out/*
# ...except the format table, which is learned from a corpus and is what makes
# rewriting byte-exact. Without it every file comes out different. It contains
# format information only — no musical content.
!out/format_table.json

# Text extracted from the official Synthstrom guidebook: third-party material,
# and reproducible from the PDF with tools/extract_guidebook.py
out/guidebook.txt
